import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 435 | Dragon Ball · Goku Predatory-Thinking Decomposition: Resource Consumption of Saiyan Combat Instinct","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 435 | Dragon Ball · Goku Predatory-Thinking Decomposition: Resource Consumption of Saiyan Combat Instinct","no":435,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Predatory Thinking","Saiyan","Combat Instinct","Goku"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","57-Dark-Replacement Body Origin and Essence"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0435_模块2-龙珠-悟空掠夺思维拆解-赛亚人战斗本能的资源消耗.md","filePath":"en/0435_模块2-龙珠-悟空掠夺思维拆解-赛亚人战斗本能的资源消耗.md"}'),a={name:"en/0435_模块2-龙珠-悟空掠夺思维拆解-赛亚人战斗本能的资源消耗.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,c,h){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-435-dragon-ball-·-goku-predatory-thinking-decomposition-resource-consumption-of-saiyan-combat-instinct" tabindex="-1">Entry 435 | Dragon Ball · Goku Predatory-Thinking Decomposition: Resource Consumption of Saiyan Combat Instinct <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-435-dragon-ball-·-goku-predatory-thinking-decomposition-resource-consumption-of-saiyan-combat-instinct" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 435 | Dragon Ball · Goku Predatory-Thinking Decomposition: Resource Consumption of Saiyan Combat Instinct&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 4) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 19, 57</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-kind-warrior-the-predatory-structure" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the kind warrior, the predatory structure <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-kind-warrior-the-predatory-structure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the kind warrior, the predatory structure&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s definition of &quot;predatory thinking&quot; does not take malice as standard, but structure: as long as a system&#39;s evolution path is built on consuming others, monopolizing resources, hoarding opportunities, however innocent and kind the protagonist himself, this thinking belongs to predation. Goku is one of comics history&#39;s kindest protagonists — he does not enslave, does not crave wealth, does not retaliate, even spared Frieza. But he stands on a predation system engine by Saiyan combat instinct without knowing. This entry, by the law-first axiom and anti-predation axiom, dissects this &quot;innocent-type predation.&quot;</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s combat instinct is itself an energy-waste device:</p><ul><li><strong>Combat consumption &gt; construction output</strong>: every Goku breakthrough is accompanied by planet-tier destruction — Namek wrecked, Earth wrecked, Supreme Kai realm wrecked — the energy he raises is far less than the energy he destroys</li><li><strong>Near-death revival&#39;s life bet</strong>: the Saiyan &quot;near-death-revival stronger&quot; mechanism essentially bets every breakthrough on &quot;can I survive this time&quot;; it is the least economical energy conversion</li><li><strong>Opponent = energy source</strong>: Goku&#39;s growth curve highly depends on &quot;a stronger villain appears&quot;; he never proactively opens a new cultivation path</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How Saiyan combat instinct feeds historical regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Planet Vegeta itself is a predatory civilization</strong>: Saiyans hired by Frieza&#39;s army to conquer planets and sell natives — this is institutionalized interstellar predation</li><li><strong>Goku continued this road</strong>: though he does not invade planets, his obsession with &quot;fighting the strong&quot; turns every crisis into a &quot;first beaten bloody, then counter-kill&quot; loop; Myriad Ranks pay blood price for his growth</li><li><strong>Combat &gt; construction values</strong>: the whole Dragon Ball world&#39;s hero standard is &quot;can fight&quot;; scientists (Bulma), scholars (Gohan forcibly pulled back to the battlefield), doctors (Bulma&#39;s healer friends) are never protagonists; civilization builders are always supporting roles</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking can be split into three layers:</p><ul><li><strong>Racial predation memory</strong>: the Saiyan race itself was Frieza&#39;s army&#39;s &quot;conquest tool&quot;; Planet Vegeta&#39;s wealth built on a hundred planets&#39; ruins. Though Goku lost his memory, he inherited this racial original sin — his &quot;combat talent&quot; itself is predatory civilization&#39;s legacy</li><li><strong>Enemy = leveling fuel</strong>: Frieza, Cell, Buu, Zamasu, Jiren… every villain&#39;s suffering history, every destroyed city, in narrative is only emotional fuel to &quot;make Goku angry, make Goku transform.&quot; Myriad Ranks&#39; blood compressed into the protagonist&#39;s power-up shot</li><li><strong>Moral leniency = immunity</strong>: Goku sparing Frieza, sparing Vegeta, sparing Buu (pure good), praised by readers as &quot;kindness.&quot; But Heng Yuan Zhou wants to ask: every villain he spared continued doing evil later (Frieza comes out again in Super to cause trouble); who pays for this &quot;kindness&quot;&#39;s price? The next batch of commoners Frieza kills</li></ul><p>Goku is not an &quot;enlightened predator,&quot; he is an <strong>&quot;innocent predator&quot;</strong> — he never questioned the loop of &quot;can&#39;t win then train more, after training fight again,&quot; never realized this loop&#39;s foundation is Myriad Ranks&#39; suffering.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Saiyan Combat Instinct</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Near-death-revival breakthrough</td><td>Life-cycle system (Doc 012); safe deduction, no life bets</td></tr><tr><td>Villain = leveling fuel</td><td>Anti-predation axiom: do not take killing-predation as evolution path; villains go reform/trial, not kill</td></tr><tr><td>Combat &gt; construction</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republican co-build: scientists, scholars, builders equal rights with warriors</td></tr><tr><td>Racial original sin inherited</td><td>Five Myriad-Ranks genealogy equal; Saiyan predatory history enshrined for reflection, not as hero narrative</td></tr><tr><td>Moral leniency = immunity</td><td>Symbiotic Court judicial independence; villain disposition goes legal process, not protagonist&#39;s whim</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Saiyan combat instinct — near-death gain, combativeness, villain stimulus curve</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;Goku does not spare Frieza,&quot; &quot;Goku refuses reconciliation with Vegeta,&quot; &quot;Goku converts combat instinct into construction labor&quot; three controls</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count subsequent cosmos-tier villain appearance frequency, Myriad-Ranks casualty rate, Goku&#39;s personal growth rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Saiyan Combat-Instinct Externality Report</em>, quantifying &quot;every time Goku transforms, how much blood price Myriad Ranks pay for it&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. Saiyan &quot;near-death-revival stronger&quot; early a rare mechanism; in Super repeatedly used by Vegeta, Gohan, Trunks; even Frieza by &quot;four months of training&quot; catches up to Super Saiyan Blue — rules completely become plot tool</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extremely high</strong>. GT&#39;s Super Saiyan 4 Saiyan-tail setting, Super&#39;s Super Saiyan God ritual, Heroes&#39;s &quot;God Blue&quot; stacking, mutually contradictory</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Goku&#39;s &quot;kindness&quot; defaulted by the whole cosmos as justice&#39;s guarantee; no one questions</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: combat consumption far exceeds construction output; all energy for &quot;fight another fight&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Saiyan race itself predatory civilization; Goku inherits the talent without reflection</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least proactively breaks predatory structure; Goku does not even reflect</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: planets conquered by Saiyans, commoners killed by villains, in narrative have no voice</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Saiyan combat instinct locked on the single line of &quot;the stronger the more can fight&quot;; no multi-path evolution</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s kindness is real, but his kindness has no structure. A good person innocently standing on predatory foundation is more dangerous than a malicious predator — because he makes predation look natural. Heng Yuan Zhou does not require Goku to become a saint, only requires him to ask: every time I get strong, whose body am I standing on? Ask this one sentence, Saiyan combat instinct truly begins to turn.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Goku predatory-thinking decomposition · resource consumption of Saiyan combat instinct described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./432_模块2-龙珠-总论悟空与战力膨胀体系定性.html">Entry 432 · Overview</a> · <a href="./460_模块2-龙珠-赛亚人设定-战斗民族的掠夺本质.html">Entry 460 · Saiyan Setting</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
